<title>USA: U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean major sales activity in the week ended Sept 5 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:  1996/97		     1997/98</p>
<p>Mexico	 59,800			   Nil</p>
<p>South Korea  53,000</p>
<p>Malaysia     41,300</p>
<p>Germany	40,600</p>
<p>Unknown	35,700</p>
<p>A total 564,300 tonnes in sales were outstanding on Aug 31 and were carried over into the new marketing year.</p>
<p>Final shipments of 239,300 tonnes brought accumulated exports for 1995/96 to 23,550,400 tonnes, slightly higher than 234,409,800 in 1994/95. The major destinations were Netherlands, Japan and Israel.</p>
<p>Exports for Sept 1-5 of 160,300 were mainly to Taiwan, Malaysia, South Korea and Mexico.</p>
</text>
